  "title": "osf doctor: read-only setup report",
  "summary": "Adds a new `osf doctor` subcommand that runs a fixed list of read-only setup checks (osf version, settings load, enabled agents and their credentials, git hooks, container detection) and prints them as text or JSON, exiting non-zero when any check fails. The new `doctor` module in the osf crate orchestrates the checks, reusing the existing `config`, `agents` and `githooks` modules; `main.rs` wires the CLI surface (`--json`, `--check`) and maps results to exit codes.",
